# Responsive breakpoints

**Phone is the default.** Base styles target the narrowest viewport with no media query. Wider breakpoints add overrides via `min-width` only — never use `max-width` for layout tiers.

Canonical tokens live in `:root` in `src/app.css` as `--bp-*`:

| Token | Value | When to use |
|-------|-------|-------------|
| *(default)* | phone | Base styles — no `@media` |
| `--bp-tablet` | `24rem` (384px) | **First** breakpoint — desktop nav, page padding, small UI fixes |
| `--bp-layout` | `40rem` (640px) | Multi-column rows, portrait beside fields, form grids |
| `--bp-desktop` | `48rem` (768px) | Wider sheet sections (story, vitality, spellcasting, modals) |
| `--bp-wide` | `72rem` (1152px) | Full page width; matches `--page-max-width` |

## Rules

1. **Never** add phone-only `max-width` overrides. Hide/show wider UI at `min-width` instead (see `.app-nav--desktop` / `.mobile-nav-toggle`).
2. In `@media`, use the **literal rem values** above — CSS variables are invalid in media queries. Add a comment: `/* --bp-tablet */`.
3. In `clamp()`, `min()`, or `max()`, you may use `var(--bp-tablet)` etc.
4. Do not add one-off breakpoints. Migrate legacy code to the nearest canonical token when touched.
5. Use `minmax(0, 1fr)` in grid columns so paired fields truncate correctly on phone.

## Examples

```css
/* ✅ phone default — mobile nav visible */
.mobile-nav-toggle {
	display: inline-flex;
}

.app-nav--desktop {
	display: none;
}

/* ✅ first breakpoint — nav + padding */
@media (min-width: 24rem) {
	/* --bp-tablet */
	.mobile-nav-toggle {
		display: none;
	}

	.app-nav--desktop {
		display: flex;
	}
}

/* ✅ layout breakpoint — multi-column */
@media (min-width: 40rem) {
	/* --bp-layout */
	.sheet-row {
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
	}
}

/* ❌ no max-width layout tiers */
@media (max-width: 23.99rem) { ... }
```
